    <h2>News</h2>    <div class="block-content">
	<ul>
	    				    				<li>
		    					    		    <h3><a href="/Online/News/New-KORA-Linux-Distro-to-Harness-the-Power-of-Local-AI">    New KORA Linux Distro to Harness the Power of Local AI</a></h3>
		    					    		        			
			        			
			    <div class="tags">
    
    		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] Artificial Intelligence', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/HPC/Artificial+Intelligence">Artificial Inte...</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[1] Operating Systems', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Operating+Systems">Operating Systems</a>
        		    </div>
		    			    <p>The development team behind CyanogenMod, Android, and Playtron unveils KORA, a Linux distribution built specifically for AI nerds.</p>
		    		</li>
			    				    				<li>
		    					    		    <h3><a href="/Online/News/Epic-Games-Targets-Linux-for-New-Launcher">    Epic Games Targets Linux for New Launcher</a></h3>
		    					    		        			
			        			
			    <div class="tags">
    
    		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] Steam', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Games/Steam">Steam</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[3] SteamOS', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Operating+Systems/Linux/SteamOS">SteamOS</a>
        		    </div>
		    			    <p>The Epic Games new launcher is still in preview, but it looks to land on several Linux distributions.</p>
		    		</li>
			    				    				<li>
		    					    		    <h3><a href="/Online/News/Fedora-45-Now-Available">    Fedora 45 Now Available</a></h3>
		    					    		        			
			        			
			    <div class="tags">
    
    		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[3] Fedora', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Operating+Systems/Linux/Fedora">Fedora</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[1] Operating Systems', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Operating+Systems">Operating Systems</a>
        		    </div>
		    			    <p>The latest iteration of Fedora has arrived with Gnome 51 and KDE Plasma 6.8.</p>
		    		</li>
			    				    				<li>
		    					    		    <h3><a href="/Online/News/Linux-7.4-is-Much-Healthier-Thanks-to-AI">    Linux 7.4 is &quot;Much Healthier&quot; Thanks to AI</a></h3>
		    					    		        			
			        			
			    <div class="tags">
    
    		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] Artificial Intelligence', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/HPC/Artificial+Intelligence">Artificial Inte...</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] Kernel', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Programming/Kernel">Kernel</a>
        		    </div>
		    			    <p>At nearly 42 million lines, Linux 7.4 is the largest merge in the kernel’s history.</p>
		    		</li>
			    				    				<li>
		    					    		    <h3><a href="/Online/News/Working-Exploit-for-a-Linux-Kernel-Flaw-Made-Public">    Working Exploit for a Linux Kernel Flaw Made Public</a></h3>
		    					    		        			
			        			
			        			
			    <div class="tags">
    
    		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] Kernel', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Programming/Kernel">Kernel</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[1] Security', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Security">Security</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] vulnerability', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Security/vulnerability">vulnerability</a>
        		    </div>
		    			    <p>Even before a bug received its CVE identifier or an upstream fix, the local privilege escalation vulnerability exploit found its way into the wild.</p>
		    		</li>
			    				    				<li>
		    					    		    <h3><a href="/Online/News/r-opensource-Bans-AI-Assisted-and-AI-Related-Projects">    r/opensource Bans AI-Assisted and AI-Related Projects</a></h3>
		    					    		        			
			        			
			        			
			    <div class="tags">
    
    		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] Artificial Intelligence', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/HPC/Artificial+Intelligence">Artificial Inte...</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[1] Community', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Community">Community</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] projects', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Community/projects">projects</a>
        		    </div>
		    			    <p>The de facto subreddit for all things open source has not only banned AI-related projects but also users who &quot;don't speak English.&quot;</p>
		    		</li>
			    				    				<li>
		    					    		    <h3><a href="/Online/News/Bottlenecks-Discovered-by-Meta-Engineers-Lead-to-Scalability-Improvements">    Bottlenecks Discovered by Meta Engineers Lead to Scalability Improvements</a></h3>
		    					    		        			
			        			
			    <div class="tags">
    
    		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] Kernel', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Programming/Kernel">Kernel</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] Performance', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/HPC/Performance">Performance</a>
        		    </div>
		    			    <p>Thanks to a small group of engineers at Meta, the Linux kernel module kernfs has been improved, which has led to some serious gains.</p>
		    		</li>
			    				    				<li>
		    					    		    <h3><a href="/Online/News/PwnEscape-Poses-VM-Vulnerability">    PwnEscape Poses VM Vulnerability</a></h3>
		    					    		        			
			        			
			        			
			    <div class="tags">
    
    		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] cyberattack', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Security/cyberattack">cyberattack</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] KVM', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Virtualization/KVM">KVM</a>
        		    , 		        	<a onclick="_gaq.push(['_trackEvent', 'taglist', '[2] vulnerability', 'text-link'])" href="/tags/view/Security/vulnerability">vulnerability</a>
        		    </div>
		    			    <p>A guest-to-host escape flaw in Linux KVM, named PwnEscape, might be yet another means of attacking Linux.</p>
		    		</li>
			    				    				<li>
